: "Vinothkumar Nagasayanan \u003ccegvinoth@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1453396 - Tests splitted into two to fix intermittent test timed out. r=ckerschb, a=test-only", "files": ["dom/base/test/mochitest.ini", "dom/base/test/test_bug704320-1.html", "dom/base/test/test_bug704320-2.html", "dom/base/test/test_bug704320.html"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "db7de5d9c65bff22de51b218fb65be81eee7bfdd", "parents": ["2b96d6f84de7aeb4b0a29e8fb9d830a10f018a70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nils Ohlmeier [:drno] \u003cdrno@ohlmeier.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1439236 - Exit early if m_copym gets called with null ptr. r=dminor, a=RyanVM\n\nCheery-picked upstream commit:\nhttps://github.com/sctplab/usrsctp/commit/d89882d04900c80860874b5eb389b3ed3a0bca3d\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 36bYbfIaqEz", "files": ["netwerk/sctp/src/user_mbuf.c"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "767ea821427e22b343932bd91af1f4cbb57a5d64", "parents": ["db7de5d9c65bff22de51b218fb65be81eee7bfdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@jesup.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1425930 - Handle Broadcast()-\u003eNotify() calling RemoveObserver(). r=froydnj, a=abillings", "files": ["xpcom/ds/Observer.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "633bd6d37172b383fc47c086aaf6df6d951c9dd5", "parents": ["767ea821427e22b343932bd91af1f4cbb57a5d64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@jesup.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463494 - Delete the sensor observerlist array in a deferred manner. r=froydnj, r=jchen, a=abillings\n\nClean up sensorlist if Dispatch fails.", "files": ["hal/Hal.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a5ab68f0fdf09446f9af2c87854018edea00b916", "parents": ["633bd6d37172b383fc47c086aaf6df6d951c9dd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Zbarsky \u003cbzbarsky@mit.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452819 - Use the right URI when getting data from the image cache for the \"Save Image As...\" context menu options. r=dao, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: zZggyJ6y7n", "files": ["browser/modules/ContextMenu.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "094590abbf52caa2634bdf09c882b05fc87b5f5c", "parents": ["a5ab68f0fdf09446f9af2c87854018edea00b916"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003cryanvm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450656 - Revert changeset b70d5eaa7921. a=jcristau", "files": ["intl/l10n/MessageContext.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "91ef127d6086546d9db3bac3343e328005718f6d", "parents": ["094590abbf52caa2634bdf09c882b05fc87b5f5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zibi Braniecki \u003czbraniecki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450656 - Canonicalize ja-JP-mac to ja-JP-macos and use BCP47 version in Fluent. r=jfkthame, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 2UbD2T8yyGm", "files": ["intl/l10n/L10nRegistry.jsm", "intl/l10n/Localization.jsm", "intl/locale/LocaleService.cpp", "intl/locale/MozLocale.cpp", "intl/locale/tests/unit/test_localeService.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "093c9b992d3a85f573c9bcdcc4ab95a03ba0180c", "parents": ["91ef127d6086546d9db3bac3343e328005718f6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1445479 - Ensure we teardown requests on image cache validation failure paths. r=tnikkel, a=jcristau\n\nIf an imgCacheValidator object is destroyed without calling\nimgCacheValidator::OnStartRequest, or imgRequest::Init fails in\nOnStartRequest, we left the bound proxies hanging on an update. Now we\ncancel the new request, and bind the validating proxies to said request\nto ensure their listeners fail gracefully.", "files": ["image/imgLoader.cpp", "image/imgLoader.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ba8bd19cb279e994d348bf5dcf67cfd73948876f", "parents": ["093c9b992d3a85f573c9bcdcc4ab95a03ba0180c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1451985 - Tell the cycle collector about ScriptLoadRequest::mElement. r=baku, a=jcristau\n\nNot doing this can cause a leak because there is a cycle between the\nload request and the script element.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: E7GbH5iDBP6", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "39832495babf66942e93b2ba210e964781db1717", "parents": ["ba8bd19cb279e994d348bf5dcf67cfd73948876f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527440720, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "55": {"changesets": [{"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1442722, bug 1455071, bug 1433642, bug 1456604, bug 1458320 - Refactor structured clone JSAPI and prevent mismatched scopes. r=jorendorff, r=baku, a=jcristau", "files": ["dom/base/StructuredCloneBlob.cpp", "dom/base/nsFrameMessageManager.cpp", "dom/base/nsStructuredCloneContainer.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IndexedDatabase.h", "dom/indexedDB/IndexedDatabaseInlines.h", "dom/ipc/StructuredCloneData.cpp", "dom/ipc/StructuredCloneData.h", "ipc/glue/IPCMessageUtils.h", "js/public/StructuredClone.h", "js/rust/src/jsglue.cpp", "js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/tests/non262/extensions/clone-errors.js", "js/src/tests/non262/extensions/clone-transferables.js", "js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManagerStartup.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1fd453ae3e9678cd50a52456ba0d1788c47d205d", "parents": ["39832495babf66942e93b2ba210e964781db1717"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527620083, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "sfink@mozilla.com"}, "56": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452653 - [wpt-reftests] Restart after audio_has_no_subtitles.html for false positive. r=jgraham, a=test-only\n\nRestart Firefox after audio_has_no_subtitles.html to prevent a false\npositive for basic.html due to bug 1463844.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 2aNPb1jk2rK", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/audio_has_no_subtitles.html.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "982e107e8c1eb6c41e15ca6f17e084be402ccc74", "parents": ["1fd453ae3e9678cd50a52456ba0d1788c47d205d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452653 - [marionette] Fix race condition for closing a browser and chrome window. r=ato, a=test-only\n\nUntil now Marionette assumed that the events `TabClose` and `unload`\nindicate that a top-level browsing context or chrome window has been\nclosed. But both events are fired when the browsing context or chrome\nwindow is about to close. As such a race condition can be seen for\nslow running builds.\n\nTo clearly wait until the top-level browsing context or chrome window\nhas been closed, the appropriate message manager needs to be observed\nfor its destroyed state.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: DCdaIiULqey", "files": ["testing/marionette/browser.js", "testing/marionette/proxy.js", "testing/marionette/sync.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "8744ef3afa008a67ad55572958addb7f5120b15f", "parents": ["982e107e8c1eb6c41e15ca6f17e084be402ccc74"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1455065 - Shell quote environment variable values when dumping them in dump_env.py. r=mshal, a=jcristau\n\nThe mozconfig output parsing code already handles shell quoted strings\nto some extent (except for bug 818377), because that's what `set`\noutputs. By quoting environment variable values, we avoid a bunch of\nproblems with \"weird\" values.", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/dump_env.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "4a61437c8f0ad49cb93543a4f6ed7ddf12c0244a", "parents": ["8744ef3afa008a67ad55572958addb7f5120b15f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Maglione \u003cmaglione.k@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1455964 - Make encodeBlob fallible on OOM. r=zombie, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 83t9c9we5zg", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManagerStartup.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9a546537d8bff630a1fbf876be55f9d599972955", "parents": ["4a61437c8f0ad49cb93543a4f6ed7ddf12c0244a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1456552 - Make Optimized MinGW builds use -O# instead of falling through and collecting a -O. r=ted, a=jcristau\n\nWe use -O2 for js (because we can) and we use -O1 for the root because there is an x86 compiler bug\nthat is not immediately bypassable\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: CnDk2ko3jfo", "files": ["js/src/old-configure.in", "old-configure.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1b10610a4e89c4b138da6d3d8084ded81dad493e", "parents": ["9a546537d8bff630a1fbf876be55f9d599972955"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Hammond \u003cmhammond@skippinet.com.au\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463624 - Ensure sync knows there is a valid user on signin. r=eoger, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 8hGU8eLYZKx", "files": ["services/sync/modules/browserid_identity.js", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_browserid_identity.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "12bf945bd10987f92e8c57d0911895ab0cdb26c8", "parents": ["1b10610a4e89c4b138da6d3d8084ded81dad493e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "J.C. Jones \u003cjjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463170 - Set AuthenticatorAssertionResponse.userHandle to null. r=ttaubert, r=smaug, a=RyanVM\n\nSummary:\nThe WebAuthn spec says to set `AuthenticatorAssertionResponse.userHandle` to\nnull when the authenticator returns no user handle (e.g., when allowList is set),\nbut we return an empty ArrayBuffer. This is because of the defaults in\nAuthenticatorAssertionResponse.h, as the field is itself unset.\n\nWe missed this change to the spec that happened in December [2], so this also\nhas a corresponding WebIDL update. I don't see any other instances of WebIDL\ndifferences.\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#ref-for-dom-authenticatorassertionresponse-userhandle%E2%91%A0\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/webauthn/commit/3b2a1d141cbd8f2954f073a6b6598d954398a986\n\nTest Plan: https://treeherder.mozilla.org/#/jobs?repo=try&revision=59a2ab255ef14e935c1aa9f457276f8e61e5d779\n\nReviewers: smaug, ttaubert\n\nBug #: 1463170\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D1337", "files": ["dom/webauthn/AuthenticatorAssertionResponse.cpp", "dom/webauthn/tests/test_webauthn_loopback.html", "dom/webidl/WebAuthentication.webidl"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "69ca265a87712c4192be6f84f12df2daee5ab5c8", "parents": ["12bf945bd10987f92e8c57d0911895ab0cdb26c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1461324 - Check for closing for-of iterators before closing a for-in one. r=arai, a=RyanVM", "files": ["js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp", "js/src/vm/Interpreter.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "7f9fbb6a71d25fd88202440ed96915f8df868a49", "parents": ["69ca265a87712c4192be6f84f12df2daee5ab5c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kris Maglione \u003cmaglione.k@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450688. r=bz, a=RyanVM\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 4KHNpxiziWd", "files": ["dom/xbl/nsXBLBinding.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "983ff6a90aae872383d52d5189396a47f3db7d17", "parents": ["7f9fbb6a71d25fd88202440ed96915f8df868a49"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527633183, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "57": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1460796 - Resolve 'Missing entry point ScriptBreak' by including usp10 for the MinGW build. r=froydnj, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: KirwpvYty5s", "files": ["js/src/old-configure.in", "old-configure.in"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fd7f1f6a44cd1005a5d4948438c20407d4eaebb6", "parents": ["983ff6a90aae872383d52d5189396a47f3db7d17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1456975 - Check fields in nsMozIconURI deserialization. r=agaynor, a=RyanVM", "files": ["image/decoders/icon/nsIconURI.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "c23f3d22028ad1d18c6e6b6dfa8970601bbc668b", "parents": ["fd7f1f6a44cd1005a5d4948438c20407d4eaebb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463884 - Part 1: Move methods only used by fontconfig backend from gfxPlatformFontList to the fontconfig subclass. (No functional change.) r=emilio, a=RyanVM", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cbe2ef9e7e4a7cb522ef9810bf79aeca628b1804", "parents": ["c23f3d22028ad1d18c6e6b6dfa8970601bbc668b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463884 - Part 2: Remove always-true argument aCheckEnvironment from gfxFcPlatformFontList::GetSampleLangForGroup. r=emilio, a=RyanVM", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5755188b40c5d312d59bacda773251d8ef34d267", "parents": ["cbe2ef9e7e4a7cb522ef9810bf79aeca628b1804"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1463884 - Part 3: Make gfxFcPlatformFontList::TryLangForGroup safe for off-main-thread use when called from GetSystemFontList. r=emilio, a=RyanVM", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "42be6252c7370b23fc143f6e4f4a6898748d822b", "parents": ["5755188b40c5d312d59bacda773251d8ef34d267"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450607 - P1. Fix constness. r=gerald, a=RyanVM\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: CeftB0qmzTf", "files": ["dom/media/MediaCache.cpp", "dom/media/MediaCache.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "fa1d57969fadfed1811b2a18efdd5c127f3ab893", "parents": ["42be6252c7370b23fc143f6e4f4a6898748d822b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450607 - P2. Synchronously seek to prepare for resuming following stop request. r=gerald, a=RyanVM\n\nBug 1415090 attempted to remove the need to access from the MediaResource members of MediaCacheStream from the main thread.\nHowever, by doing so the logic flow for resuming the channel changed from a synchronous access to an asynchronous one.\nThis changed some assumptions and allowed the ChannelMediaResource to be used before the Seek call completed.\n\nFor now, re-add a cross thread access to the MediaCacheStream. A more elegant fix will be worked on in bug 1464045\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 2xBTjDEqrkI", "files": ["dom/media/ChannelMediaResource.cpp", "dom/media/MediaCache.cpp", "dom/media/MediaCache.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "27ec43a60a397c61b9951e1398aaeed2bcf96934", "parents": ["fa1d57969fadfed1811b2a18efdd5c127f3ab893"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450607 - P3. Remove unused argument. r=gerald, a=RyanVM\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 6NU9BLJi6kl", "files": ["dom/media/ChannelMediaResource.cpp", "dom/media/MediaCache.cpp", "dom/media/MediaCache.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "83f865afba050de072c57aee10920af07c9d8d43", "parents": ["27ec43a60a397c61b9951e1398aaeed2bcf96934"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527633632, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "58": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nick Thomas \u003cnthomas@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1462120 - Update verify fixes for ESR60 branch, r=bhearsum a=release  DONTBUILD", "files": ["taskcluster/ci/release-update-verify-config/kind.yml", "taskcluster/ci/release-update-verify/kind.yml", "taskcluster/taskgraph/transforms/update_verify_config.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/release/update-verify-config-creator.py"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ba558623bafd83c5b113d2072f7ef23653c3bb4c", "parents": ["83f865afba050de072c57aee10920af07c9d8d43"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527637316, "git_changesets": [null], "user": "nthomas@mozilla.com"}, "59": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1465108 - Fix count of compacting update tasks started r=sfink a=abillings a=RyanVM", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "095a9b56bb34649dea0e9bb8f38b523e33c3c9c0", "parents": ["ba558623bafd83c5b113d2072f7ef23653c3bb4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1465108 - Use function pointers rather than virtual run method for GC parallel tasks r=sfink a=abillings a=RyanVM", "files": ["js/src/gc/Allocator.cpp", "js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCParallelTask.h", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/gc/Statistics.h", "js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "6983f5845e9bb0cc79ee9eafb017f41a652970ad", "parents": ["095a9b56bb34649dea0e9bb8f38b523e33c3c9c0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527675301, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "jcoppeard@mozilla.com"}, "60": {"changesets": [{"author": "Justin Wood \u003cCallek@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1455100 - Make devedition its own language pack addon id, by using MOZ_LANGPACK_EID again. r=nalexander, r=Pike, a=RyanVM\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: z1SJmCQflq", "files": ["browser/locales/Makefile.in", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/langpack_manifest.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/action/test_langpack_manifest.py", "toolkit/locales/l10n.mk"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "164918e56cb9029ab6d72f535ba6955f8fbc9021", "parents": ["6983f5845e9bb0cc79ee9eafb017f41a652970ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1459693 - Ensure the right anonymous element is focused when calling input.focus(). r=mccr8, a=RyanVM", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "34f8ad2b2793b07948c4a69682d76b192a4cc6cf", "parents": ["164918e56cb9029ab6d72f535ba6955f8fbc9021"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1457281 - Remove dom.ipc.scheduler pref. r=froydnj, a=RyanVM\n\nThe JS engine has changed the APIs that cooperative scheduling relies\non into immediate crashes. Some users seem to set the prefs, and then\nwe get a lot of crashes on Nightly. This removes the top-level pref to\nsave them some grief.\n\nI continue to pass the pref as false to the child process to avoid\nweirdness if we somehow we get this far when the parent and child have\ndifferent versions.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 3o3yV2efx2r", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/all.js", "xpcom/threads/Scheduler.cpp", "xpcom/threads/Scheduler.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "5a41bf296a861f25c9846b22a4b600f00e26e647", "parents": ["34f8ad2b2793b07948c4a69682d76b192a4cc6cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452090 - Only enable handle verifier on 32-bit Nightly and debug builds. r=jimm, a=RyanVM\n\nThis also adds the ability to enable it using the environement variable\nMOZ_ENABLE_HANDLE_VERIFIER.", "files": ["security/sandbox/win/SandboxInitialization.cpp", "toolkit/xre/test/win/TestDllInterceptor.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e85d91afc9a3e47595a6031612a20b33fdd50483", "parents": ["5a41bf296a861f25c9846b22a4b600f00e26e647"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Chimento \u003cphilip.chimento@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1464912 - Add exposeToActiveJS specialization for JSString. r=sfink, a=RyanVM", "files": ["js/public/RootingAPI.h"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "dc880f246c3ec0710811efeb614be76099ee45b5", "parents": ["e85d91afc9a3e47595a6031612a20b33fdd50483"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527706675, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "61": {"changesets": [{"author": "Shane Caraveo \u003cscaraveo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1403965 - Fix context menu position in extension sidebar. r=kmag, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 37XgWflt2qG", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/base/content/webext-panels.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "788dd61d4625e176bfef64d54e6bf71ebdaf2905", "parents": ["dc880f246c3ec0710811efeb614be76099ee45b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1435615 - Reuse the same process when loading URIs on about:newtab when requests have POST data. r=mconley, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 201VupYACvX", "files": ["toolkit/modules/E10SUtils.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a41872ae8adb19002a7416146299ce4c0f5d0c8a", "parents": ["788dd61d4625e176bfef64d54e6bf71ebdaf2905"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1442195 - Don't crash when finding an unexpected default font type. r=xidorn, a=jcristau\n\nFor now just return sans-serif, though as the FIXME comment indicates we should\nprobably just carry around the font-name instead.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: CIPbV3R5Ul", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/gecko.mako.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "9587d5f8a452b9ea73181cb72846956c0242bf2c", "parents": ["a41872ae8adb19002a7416146299ce4c0f5d0c8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johann Hofmann \u003cjhofmann@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1450448 - Correctly handle non-initialized appCache in site data preferences. r=Gijs, a=jcristau\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: IhQGAWNQtR0", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/SiteDataManager.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "d6d4fa13e5c885a8cd014aeea236e7b9f85df0f8", "parents": ["9587d5f8a452b9ea73181cb72846956c0242bf2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike de Boer \u003cmdeboer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1434252 - nsICookieService may throw an error in certain circumstances, so let's make SessionCookies::restore infallible. r=dao, a=jcristau\n\nPlease see bug 1462402 for more details and the root cause.\nSessionCookies.jsm uses nsICookieService::CookieExists and nsICookieService::Add\nto restore session-cookies. These currently throw for hostnames that contain a\nleading '.' and maybe other cases, so we need to wrap the calls in a try..catch\nblock to prevent breakage, leading to an unrestored session.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: 9gZ7K6lwcQF", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionCookies.jsm"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a53b5d718e8532482f086a7819c81e73a247f379", "parents": ["d6d4fa13e5c885a8cd014aeea236e7b9f85df0f8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1527815755, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "62": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas B. Pierron \u003cnicolas.b.pierron@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1464829 - Ensure the recover instruction vector has the expected size. r=jandem, a=jcristau", "files": ["js/src/jit/JSJitFrameIter.h", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "eab56078999a914abc3cf9ac16ca2ca7c06548d8", "parents": ["a53b5d718e8532482f086a7819c81e73a247f379"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jmuizelaar@mozilla.com", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452375 - ssse3-scaler: handle init failure. r=sotaro, a=abillings", "files": ["gfx/2d/ssse3-scaler.c", "gfx/2d/ssse3-scaler.h", "gfx/layers/basic/BasicCompositor.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "cbf5d1ea2f9ac44be54ead384af566236752ad18", "parents": ["eab56078999a914abc3cf9ac16ca2ca7c06548d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jmuizelaar@mozilla.com", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452375 - sse3-scaler: make sure iter-\u003ex/y is representable. r=sotaro, a=abillings", "files": ["gfx/2d/ssse3-scaler.c"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "e205f08f30a726cc6edbb53ae4aa1bf438e4ffc5", "parents": ["cbf5d1ea2f9ac44be54ead384af566236752ad18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1461268 - P1. Disable AMD VP9 decoder. r=bryce, a=jcristau\n\nIt has greatly regressed with recent AMD drivers, providing worse performance than the software decoder under most circumstances.\n\nMozReview-Commit-ID: Jtabi1qhoYF", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPrefs.h", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "0e83c9c98b6c55e0b5500dec8aba2164ca38d546", "parents": ["e205f08f30a726cc6edbb53ae4aa1bf438e4ffc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjyavenard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1461268 - P2. Bump benchmark version ID. r=bryce, a=jcristau\n\nThis will force the benchmark to be re-run, f